lf from the owner goals and actual dependencies.\n\nOwner priorities and constraints: minimize QPBT critical-path duration and maximize useful parallelism; primary relay only; gpt-6-astra max for every project session; fan-out disabled. The owner explicitly removed reservations for FV, LDT-Lean-Paper, and the old /home/drx session, allowing11 project workers plus main. Keep those other sessions untouched, preserve the future explicit primary/both toggle, and apply normal integrity/review/merge rules. This quota instruction does not decide pending owner blockerB7.\n\nSTANDING OWNER FLOOR: Maintain8--11 useful live QPBT workers, excluding main. Anticipate completions and replenish promptly with real independent work; do not count idle reservations, duplicate writers or completed sessions. If a concrete dependency or service constraint prevents the floor, report it explicitly. This floor does not override proof budgets, review caps, account limits or normal validation.\n\nLATEST OWNER INBOX CORRECTION (recorded2026-09-06T02:58:41Z): Main decides routine blockers BEFORE escalation and sends only the highest-risk blockers to issue26. ANY item already posted in issue26, including B7, MUST WAIT for the human owner decision. The earlier delegation of existing inbox items is withdrawn. No approval may be inferred from the worker-floor, quota or role instructions. Meta remains guidance-only; main owns planning and assignments.\n\nLATEST OWNER EFFORT UPDATE (recorded2026-09-06T03:26:22Z): Main stays max. All new/resumed subagents stay gpt-6-astra on primary relay, but main chooses max OR xhigh according to role, task difficulty, observed quality and latency. Earlier mandatory-max-for-every-worker clauses are superseded. Dispatcher and runtime shims must honor the selection. Record effort and rationale, elapsed time, available token usage, outcome and review findings; distinguish configured from server-verified effort. Learn through useful work only, without benchmark or filler