r, def:expanded-state,\\\\n   268\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tlem:qld-4-7}\\\\n   269\\\\t\\\\tFor either player and either Pauli basis, the non-encoding marginal mass in\\\\n   270\\\\t\\\\tEquation~\\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-nonencoding-mass} is at most\\\\n   271\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\delta_P^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{supp}}=C_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{supp}}B$ for a universal\\\\n   272\\\\t\\\\t$C_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{supp}}\\\\\\\\geq1$. This bound must be derived from point consistency and\\\\n   273\\\\t\\\\tSchwartz--Zippel; it is not an additional extraction hypothesis.\\\\n   274\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   275\\\\t\\\\n   276\\\\t% Following the source, the next lemma is stated after\\\\n   277\\\\t% lem:qld-construct-the-paulis, whose proof invokes it; its own proof\\\\n   278\\\\t% depends only on lem:qld-4-7 and lem:qld-comm-cons, so there is no\\\\n   279\\\\t% circularity.\\\\n   280\\\\tLemmas~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7} and~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-comm-cons} imply the following two estimates, which were used in the proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-construct-the-paulis}.\\\\n   281\\\\t\\\\n   282\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[The marginals absorb the point measurements]\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-constructing-the-paulis-helper}\\\\n   283\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.sum_marginalPoly_pointMeas_approx_id}\\\\n   284\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.marginalPoly_sub_pointMeas_approx_zero}\\\\n   285\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanok\\\\n   286\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:s-w-marginals, def:expanded-point-measurement, def:expanded-state, def:povm-distance, lem:qld-4-7, def:symmetric-equivalents}\\\\n   287\\\\t\\\\tFor $W \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{X,Z\\\\\\\\}$, on average over uniformly random $u \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q^m$,\\\\n   288\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{equation}\\\\\\\\label{eq:qld-sg-cons}\\\\n   289\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\sum_g (\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_g)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_{g(u)})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''} \\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\delta_P^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{id}}} \\\\\\\\Id\\\\n   290\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{equation}\\\\n   291\\\\t\\\\tand\\\\n   292\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{equation}\\\\\\\\label{eq:qld-sg-cons2}\\\\n   293\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\bigl(\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_g \\\\\\\\cdot (\\\\\\\\Id - \\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_{g(u)})\\\\\\\\bigr)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\delta_P^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ann}}} 0\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   294\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{equation}\\\\n   295\\\\t\\\\twhere the answer summation is over $g \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\mathrm{ideg}_{d,m}(\\\\\\\\F_q)$. The independently quantified scale $\\\\\\\\delta_P^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ann}}$ includes the additional point-measurement error in \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-sg-cons2}. Furthermore, all symmetric equivalents of these approximations also hold (Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:symmetric-equivalents}).\\\\n   296\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   297\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{proof}\\\\n   298\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{lem:qld-4-7, fact:agreement, fact:add-a-proj, def:bracket, lem:qld-comm-cons}\\\\n   299\\\\t\\\\tThe point-consistency conclusion of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7} states that, on average over $u \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q^m$,\\\\n   300\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   301\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi} \\\\\\\\sum_g (\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_g)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_{g(u)})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi} \\\\\\\\geq 1 - \\\\\\\\delta_G\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   302\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   303\\\\t\\\\twhich says exactly that the operator on the left-hand side of \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-sg-cons} is $\\\\\\\\delta_G$-consistent with $\\\\\\\\Id$; Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{fact:agreement} and the universal-factor enlargement give the $\\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\delta_P}$ statement \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-sg-cons}. For \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-sg-cons2}, the same consistency, written with the coarse-graining $\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_{[g(u)=a]} = \\\\\\\\sum_{g : g(u) = a} \\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_g$ as $(\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_{[g(u)=a]})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\approx_{O(\\\\\\\\delta_G)} (\\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_{a})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''}$ with answer summation over $a \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q$, is left-multiplied by $(\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_{[g(u)=a]})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'}$ using Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{fact:add-a-proj}; moving $\\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_a$ from registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''$ to $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'$ costs a further $\\\\\\\\eps$ by Cauchy--Schwarz together with the self-consistency of the $\\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_a$ (Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-comm-cons}), giving\\\\n   304\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   305\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t(\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_{[g(u)=a]})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\approx_{O(\\\\\\\\delta_G + \\\\\\\\eps)} (\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_{[g(u)=a]} \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_{a})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'}\\\\\\\\;.\\\\n   306\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   307\\\\t\\\\tExpanding\\\\n   308\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   309\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\E_u \\\\\\\\sum_g \\\\\\\\bigl\\\\\\\\| (\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_{g} \\\\\\\\cdot (\\\\\\\\Id - \\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_{g(u)}))_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi} \\\\\\\\bigr\\\\\\\\|^2\\\\n   310\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t= \\\\\\\\E_u \\\\\\\\sum_a \\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi} \\\\\\\\bigl((\\\\\\\\Id - \\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_{a}) \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_{[g(u)=a]} \\\\\\\\cdot (\\\\\\\\Id - \\\\\\\\hat{M}^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point}, W), u}_{a})\\\\\\\\bigr)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi}\\\\n   311\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   312\\\\t\\\\tand bounding the right-hand side by $O(\\\\\\\\delta_G + \\\\\\\\eps)$ using the two approximations above yields \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-sg-cons2} at scale $\\\\\\\\delta_P$. The symmetric equivalents follow by the same argument with the register bipartitions interchanged.\\\\n   313\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{proof}\\\\n   314\\\\t\\\\n   315\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{The swap unitaries and the extraction of the Pauli group}\\\\n   316\\\\t\\\\n   317\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{definition}[The swap unitaries]\\\\\\\\label{def:v-swap-unitary}\\\\n   318\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.swapUnitary}\\\\n   319\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanok\\\\n   320\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{lem:qld-4-7, def:generalized-pauli, def:qld-full-field-decoder}\\\\n   321\\\\t\\\\tDefine the linear map\\\\n   322\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   323\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tV_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} = \\\\\\\\sum_{g_X,g_Z} (\\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\bigl(\\\\\\\\tau^X(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_Z)) \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^Z(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_X))\\\\\\\\bigr)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''}\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   324\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   325\\\\t\\\\twhere $\\\\\\\\tau^X(\\\\\\\\cdot)$ and $\\\\\\\\tau^Z(\\\\\\\\cdot)$ are the generalized Pauli observables acting on $(\\\\\\\\C^q)^{\\\\\\\\ot M}$; note that the argument of $\\\\\\\\tau^X$ is $\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_Z)$ and the argument of $\\\\\\\\tau^Z$ is $\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_X)$. The map $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}$, acting on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''$, is defined analogously.\\\\n   326\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{definition}\\\\n   327\\\\t\\\\n   328\\\\t% In the source the following properties are established inline with the\\\\n   329\\\\t% definition of the swap unitaries; they are recorded here as a lemma.\\\\n   330\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[Unitarity and conjugation action of the swap unitaries]\\\\\\\\label{lem:v-swap-conjugation}\\\\n   331\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.swapUnitary_mul_conjTranspose}\\\\n   332\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.conjTranspose_mul_swapUnitary}\\\\n   333\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.swapUnitary_conj_tildeObs}\\\\n   334\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.swapUnitary_conj_tildeM}\\\\n   335\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanok\\\\n   336\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:v-swap-unitary, def:tilde-w-observables, def:tilde-m-measurement, def:generalized-pauli, def:indicator-vector, def:bracket}\\\\n   337\\\\t\\\\tThe maps $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}$ and $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}$ of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:v-swap-unitary} are unitaries acting on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''$ and $\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''$ respectively, and their conjugation action is exact, as follows. For all $W \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{X,Z\\\\\\\\}$, $j \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{0,\\\\\\\\ldots,t-1\\\\\\\\}$, and $\\\\\\\\tilde{u} \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q^M$,\\\\n   338\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{equation}\\\\\\\\label{eq:v-swap-obs-conjugation}\\\\n   339\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tV_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tilde{W}^j(\\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\, V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}^\\\\\\\\dagger = \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\bigl( \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\bigr)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''}\\\\n   340\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\qquad \\\\\\\\text{and} \\\\\\\\qquad\\\\n   341\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tV_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}} \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tilde{W}^j(\\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\, V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}^\\\\\\\\dagger = \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\bigl( \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\bigr)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''}\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   342\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{equation}\\\\n   343\\\\t\\\\tand for all $W \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{X,Z\\\\\\\\}$, $u \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q^m$, and $a \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q$,\\\\n   344\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{equation}\\\\\\\\label{eq:qld-unitary-6}\\\\n   345\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tV_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}} \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tilde{M}^{W,\\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u)}_a \\\\\\\\, V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}^\\\\\\\\dagger = \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'} \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\tau^W_{[g_h(u)=a]})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''}\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   346\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\qquad\\\\n   347\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\tau^W_{[g_h(u)=a]} = \\\\\\\\sum_{h \\\\\\\\,:\\\\\\\\, g_h(u) = a} \\\\\\\\tau^W_h\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   348\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{equation}\\\\n   349\\\\t\\\\ttogether with the analogous identity for $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}$ on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''$.\\\\n   350\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   351\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{proof}\\\\n   352\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{lem:qld-4-7, lem:tildew-product-form, lem:twisted-commutation, def:v-swap-unitary, def:tilde-m-measurement, def:tau-dot-product-projector, def:indicator-vector, def:decoding-map, def:generalized-pauli}\\\\n   353\\\\t\\\\tSince the measurement $\\\\\\\\{\\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}\\\\\\\\}$ is projective (Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}) and the $\\\\\\\\tau^X, \\\\\\\\tau^Z$ observables are self-inverse,\\\\n   354\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   355\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tV_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}^\\\\\\\\dagger = \\\\\\\\sum_{g_X,g_Z} (\\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''} = \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''}\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   356\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   357\\\\t\\\\tand the same computation gives $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}^\\\\\\\\dagger V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} = \\\\\\\\Id$, so $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}$ is unitary; likewise $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}$. For \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:v-swap-obs-conjugation}, conjugate the product form \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:tildewj-product-form} of $\\\\\\\\tilde{W}^j(\\\\\\\\tilde{u})$ (Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:tildew-product-form}): by the orthogonality of the projectors $\\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}$, only the diagonal terms survive, and the twisted commutation relation (Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:twisted-commutation})\\\\n   358\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   359\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\tau^X(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_Z)) \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^Z(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_X)) \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u}) = (-1)^{\\\\\\\\tr( e_j(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_W) \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\tilde{u}))} \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^X(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_Z)) \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^Z(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_X))\\\\n   360\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   361\\\\t\\\\tcancels the sign $(-1)^{\\\\\\\\tr(e_j (\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g_W) \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\tilde{u}))}$ term by term, leaving $\\\\\\\\sum_{g_X,g_Z} \\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u}) = \\\\\\\\Id \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u})$. For \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-unitary-6}, expand $\\\\\\\\tilde{M}^{W,\\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u)}_a$ by \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:tilde_M} and \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:def-tauwu}; by the orthogonality of the $\\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}$, conjugation replaces, in the term of $\\\\\\\\hat{S}^W_g$, each projector $\\\\\\\\tau^W_h$ by $\\\\\\\\tau^W_{h + \\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g)}$, using the identities $\\\\\\\\tau^X(s)\\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^Z_h \\\\\\\\,\\\\\\\\tau^X(s)^\\\\\\\\dagger = \\\\\\\\tau^Z_{h+s}$ and $\\\\\\\\tau^Z(s)\\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^X_h\\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^Z(s)^\\\\\\\\dagger = \\\\\\\\tau^X_{h+s}$. Substituting $h' = h + \\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g)$ turns the constraint $h \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u) = (\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g) \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u)) - a$ into $h' \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u) = -a = a$, since $\\\\\\\\F_q$ has characteristic $2$; the quantity $\\\\\\\\mathrm{Dec}(g) \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u)$ cancels exactly, so no relation between it and $g(u)$ is used (Remark~\\\\\\\\ref{rem:qld-decoding-identity}). Since $h' \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u) = g_{h'}(u)$ \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:low-degree-encoding-definition}, summing over $g$ gives \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-unitary-6}; the computation for $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}$ on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''$ is identical.\\\\n   362\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{proof}\\\\n   363\\\\t\\\\n   364\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[Extraction of the EPR state and the Pauli observables]\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-unitary}\\\\n   365\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.ExtractionWitness}\\\\n   366\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.deltaExtract}\\\\n   367\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{lem:qld-4-7, def:v-swap-unitary, def:expanded-state, lem:projective-strategy-setup, def:generalized-pauli, def:EPR, def:povm-distance}\\\\n   368\\\\t\\\\tThere is a universal constant $C_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}}\\\\\\\\geq1$. Set\\\\n   369\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   370\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\delta_P^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}}=C_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}}B,\\\\n   371\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\qquad\\\\n   372\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{qld}}=C_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}}\\\\n   373\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\left((\\\\\\\\delta_P^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}})^{1/4}+\\\\\\\\frac{md}{q}\\\\\\\\right).\\\\n   374\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   375\\\\t\\\\tThere exist unitaries $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}$ acting on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''$ and $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}$ acting on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''$, such that the following hold.\\\\n   376\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{enumerate}\\\\n   377\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\item There exists a state $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}}$ on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'$ such that\\\\n   378\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   379\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\bigl\\\\\\\\| V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} \\\\\\\\ot V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat{\\\\\\\\psi}}_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''} - \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}}_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M}_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''} \\\\\\\\bigr\\\\\\\\|^2 \\\\\\\\leq \\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{qld}}\\\\\\\\;.\\\\n   380\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   381\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\item For $W \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{X,Z\\\\\\\\}$,\\\\n   382\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{align*}\\\\n   383\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tV_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\bigl(M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h \\\\\\\\bigr)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} \\\\\\\\, V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}^\\\\\\\\dagger &\\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{qld}}} \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'} \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\tau^W_h)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''}\\\\\\\\;, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   384\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tV_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}} \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\bigl(M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h \\\\\\\\bigr)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}} \\\\\\\\, V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}^\\\\\\\\dagger &\\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{qld}}} \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'} \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\tau^W_h)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''}\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n   385\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{align*}\\\\n   386\\\\t\\\\t\\\\twhere the $\\\\\\\\approx$ statements hold with respect to the state $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}}_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M}_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''}$, with the answer summation over $h \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q^{M}$ and no average over questions.\\\\n   387\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{enumerate}\\\\n   388\\\\t\\\\tThe unitaries may be taken to be $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}$ and $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}$ of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:v-swap-unitary}.\\\\n   389\\\\t\\\\tNo Lean declaration states this lemma. The only existence declaration available assumes the global polynomial-pair measurement of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7} as data, instead of obtaining it from that lemma as the proof below does; it is therefore a conditional helper, it does not certify the statement above, and it is not linked here. It is recorded instead in the formalization-support node Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary-given-global-pair} below, as the proof-gap protocol requires. The discrepancy and the source-facing declaration that must replace it are recorded in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_extraction-transfer}.\\\\n   390\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   391\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{proof}\\\\n   392\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:v-swap-unitary, lem:v-swap-conjugation, lem:tildew-product-form, lem:qld-construct-the-paulis, lem:qld-win-implications, fact:triangle-for-simeq, def:bracket, lem:cancellation, lem:schwartz-zippel-total-degree, lem:qld-4-7}\\\\n   393\\\\t\\\\tFor the first item, the self-consistency of the observables $\\\\\\\\tilde{W}^j$ (Item~2 of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-construct-the-paulis}) is equivalent, since these observables are Hermitian involutions (Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:tildew-product-form}), to $\\\\\\\\E_{j \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{0,\\\\\\\\ldots,t-1\\\\\\\\}} \\\\\\\\E_{\\\\\\\\tilde{u} \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q^M} \\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi} \\\\\\\\tilde{W}^j(\\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tilde{W}^j(\\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi} \\\\\\\\geq 1 - \\\\\\\\delta_P/2$; setting $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} = V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} \\\\\\\\ot V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi}$ and using the exact conjugation identities of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:v-swap-conjugation}, this becomes $\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\vartheta} H_W \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\geq 1 - \\\\\\\\delta_P/2$ for $W \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{X,Z\\\\\\\\}$, where $H_W = \\\\\\\\E_j \\\\\\\\E_{\\\\\\\\tilde{u}} \\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u}) \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tau^W(e_j \\\\\\\\tilde{u}) = \\\\\\\\bigl( \\\\\\\\E_{s \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q} \\\\\\\\tau^W(s) \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tau^W(s) \\\\\\\\bigr)^{\\\\\\\\ot M}$ by the tensor factorization of $\\\\\\\\tau^W(\\\\\\\\tilde{u})$ and the invariance of the uniform average over $s$ under $s \\\\\\\\mapsto e_j s$. By Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:cancellation}, $\\\\\\\\E_{s,s'} \\\\\\\\tau^X(s)\\\\\\\\tau^Z(s') \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tau^X(s)\\\\\\\\tau^Z(s') = \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}$ on each pair of qudits, whence $H_X H_Z = \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M}$. The bounds $\\\\\\\\| (\\\\\\\\Id - H_W)\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\|^2 \\\\\\\\leq \\\\\\\\delta_P$ and $\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\vartheta} H_W^2 \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\geq 1 - 2\\\\\\\\delta_P$, combined through the triangle inequality $\\\\\\\\| H_X \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} - H_Z \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\| \\\\\\\\leq 2\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P}$ (see Remark~\\\\\\\\ref{rem:qld-unitary-triangle-slip}), give $\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\Id_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'} \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\geq 1 - 4\\\\\\\\delta_P$.\\\\n   394\\\\t\\\\t% Case distinction added: the source normalizes the projected vector\\\\n   395\\\\t\\\\t% without ensuring that it is nonzero; see Remark rem:qld-unitary-triangle-slip.\\\\n   396\\\\t\\\\tIf $\\\\\\\\delta_P > 1/8$, then, after enlarging the universal constant in $\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{qld}}$, both items of the lemma hold with $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}}$ an arbitrary unit state, since their left-hand sides never exceed $4$; assume therefore $\\\\\\\\delta_P \\\\\\\\leq 1/8$. Then the vector $(\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta}$ has squared norm at least $1 - 4\\\\\\\\delta_P \\\\\\\\geq 1/2 > 0$, and $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}}$ may be defined as its normalization; the overlap of $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta}$ with $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M}$ equals the norm of that vector and is at least $\\\\\\\\sqrt{1 - 4\\\\\\\\delta_P} \\\\\\\\geq 1 - 4\\\\\\\\delta_P$, which yields the first item with a bound of $8\\\\\\\\delta_P = O(\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P})$. For the second item, Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-win-implications} gives, on average over $u \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q^m$, $M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_{[g_h(u)=a]} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\Id \\\\\\\\simeq_\\\\\\\\eps \\\\\\\\Id \\\\\\\\ot M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_a$ and $\\\\\\\\Id \\\\\\\\ot M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_a \\\\\\\\simeq_\\\\\\\\eps M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Point},W),u}_a \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\Id$, where $M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_{[g_h(u)=a]} = \\\\\\\\sum_{h : g_h(u) = a} M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h$; combining these with Item~1 of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-construct-the-paulis} by Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{fact:triangle-for-simeq}, using $\\\\\\\\eps \\\\\\\\leq \\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\eps} \\\\\\\\leq \\\\\\\\delta_P$, yields $M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_{[g_h(u)=a]} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\Id \\\\\\\\simeq_{\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P}} \\\\\\\\Id \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tilde{M}^{W,\\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u)}_a$. Writing $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\Delta} = \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M}$, the quantity to be bounded for the $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}$-side relation equals $2 - 2\\\\\\\\sum_h \\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\Delta} V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_h V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}^\\\\\\\\dagger \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\tau^W_h)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\Delta}$, since $(\\\\\\\\tau^W_h)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M} = (\\\\\\\\tau^W_h)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M}$. Replacing $(\\\\\\\\tau^W_h)_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''}$ by the averaged coarse-graining $\\\\\\\\E_u \\\\\\\\sum_{h' : g_{h'}(u) = g_h(u)} (\\\\\\\\tau^W_{h'})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''}$ costs at most $md/q$ by Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:schwartz-zippel-total-degree} (distinct $h \\\\\\\\neq h'$ have distinct encodings $g_h \\\\\\\\neq g_{h'}$, of total degree at most $md$), and by \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-unitary-6} the resulting sum equals $\\\\\\\\E_u \\\\\\\\sum_{a} \\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\Delta} V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}} M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_{[g_h(u)=a]} V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}^\\\\\\\\dagger \\\\\\\\ot V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}} \\\\\\\\tilde{M}^{W,\\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u)}_a V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}^\\\\\\\\dagger \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\Delta}$. Exchanging $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\Delta}$ for $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta}$ costs $O(\\\\\\\\delta_P^{1/4})$ by the first item, and the resulting expression $\\\\\\\\E_u \\\\\\\\sum_a \\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi} M^{(\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli},W)}_{[g_h(u)=a]} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\tilde{M}^{W,\\\\\\\\mathrm{ind}_m(u)}_a \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat\\\\\\\\psi}$ is at least $1 - O(\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P})$ by the $\\\\\\\\simeq_{\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P}}$ relation above. Altogether the distance is $O(\\\\\\\\delta_P^{1/4} + md/q)$; the $\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}$-side relation is proved identically.\\\\n   397\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{proof}\\\\n   398\\\\t\\\\n   399\\\\t% This support node records a conditional Lean helper; it is not a statement\\\\n   400\\\\t% from the paper.\\\\n   401\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[Formalization support for Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary}]\\\\n   402\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-unitary-given-global-pair}\\\\n   403\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_extractionWitness}\\\\n   404\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanok\\\\n   405\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{lem:qld-4-7, def:v-swap-unitary, def:expanded-state, lem:projective-strategy-setup, def:generalized-pauli, def:EPR, def:povm-distance}\\\\n   406\\\\t\\\\tThis formalization-only auxiliary is not a named statement of the paper. It is the conditional, given-witness form of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary}: the projective global polynomial-pair measurement $\\\\\\\\{\\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}\\\\\\\\}$ of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, together with the two point-consistency estimates that lemma asserts at a parameter $\\\\\\\\delta_G \\\\\\\\geq 0$, is assumed as data rather than obtained from that lemma. There is a universal constant $C_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}} \\\\\\\\geq 1$ such that the following holds for every admissible $(q,m,d)$, every $0 \\\\\\\\leq \\\\\\\\eps \\\\\\\\leq 1$, every projective strategy setup at error $\\\\\\\\eps$ (Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:projective-strategy-setup}), every $\\\\\\\\delta_G \\\\\\\\geq 0$, and every assumed measurement as above. The swap unitaries $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}}$ and $V_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}}$ built from that measurement by Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:v-swap-unitary} are two-sided unitaries, and there is a normalized state $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\mathrm{aux}}$ on registers $\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}'\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}'$ for which items 1 and 2 of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary} hold at the scale $\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{qld}}$ of that lemma, computed from $\\\\\\\\eps$ and the assumed $\\\\\\\\delta_G$.\\\\n   407\\\\t\\\\tThe statement-level mark records that the linked declaration has exactly this shape, assumed measurement included; it does not certify Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary}, whose proof obtains that measurement from Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}. By the criterion of the proof-gap protocol the assumed measurement is proof debt rather than a faithful boundary hypothesis. The source-facing declaration that must replace it, and the correction of the linked declaration's name and docstring, which still describe it as source-facing, are recorded in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_extraction-transfer}.\\\\n   408\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   409\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{proof}\\\\n   410\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:v-swap-unitary, lem:v-swap-conjugation, lem:tildew-product-form, lem:qld-construct-the-paulis, lem:qld-win-implications, fact:triangle-for-simeq, def:bracket, lem:cancellation, lem:schwartz-zippel-total-degree}\\\\n   411\\\\t\\\\tThe proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary} above, with its appeal to Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7} replaced by the assumed measurement. The proof of the linked declaration is open, so no proof-level mark is placed here.\\\\n   412\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{proof}\\\\n   413\\\\t\\\\n   414\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[Preservation of the robustness error family]\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-extraction-error-form}\\\\n   415\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.deltaExtract_le_deltaQld}\\\\n   416\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:admissible, lem:qld-unitary}\\\\n   417\\\\t\\\\tLet $C\\\\\\\\geq1$, $a>1$, and $0<b<1$. Suppose that\\\\n   418\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   419\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\delta_G=a(md)^a\\\\\\\\bigl(\\\\\\\\eps^b+q^{-b}+2^{-bmd}\\\\\\\\bigr),\\\\n   420\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\qquad\\\\n   421\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\delta_P=C\\\\\\\\left(\\\\\\\\delta_G+\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\eps}+\\\\\\\\frac{md}{q}\\\\\\\\right),\\\\n   422\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   423\\\\t\\\\tand set $\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}}=C(\\\\\\\\delta_P^{1/4}+md/q)$. There are constants\\\\n   424\\\\t\\\\t$a'\\\\\\\\geq1$ and $0<b'<1$, depending only on $C,a,b$, such that, for every\\\\n   425\\\\t\\\\tadmissible $(q,m,d)$ and every $0\\\\\\\\leq\\\\\\\\eps\\\\\\\\leq1$,\\\\n   426\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n   427\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ext}}\\\\n   428\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\leq a'(md)^{a'}\\\\\\\\bigl(\\\\\\\\eps^{b'}+q^{-b'}+2^{-b'md}\\\\\\\\bigr).\\\\n   429\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n   430\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   431\\\\t\\\\n   432\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{remark}[Two steps in the source proof of the extraction lemma]\\\\\\\\label{rem:qld-unitary-triangle-slip}\\\\n   433\\\\t\\\\tIn the source proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary}, the triangle inequality gives $\\\\\\\\| H_X \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} - H_Z \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\| \\\\\\\\leq \\\\\\\\| (\\\\\\\\Id - H_X)\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\| + \\\\\\\\| (\\\\\\\\Id - H_Z)\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\| \\\\\\\\leq 2\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P}$, so that $\\\\\\\\| H_X \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} - H_Z \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta} \\\\\\\\|^2 \\\\\\\\leq 4\\\\\\\\delta_P$; the source instead asserts the bound $2\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P}$ for the \\\\\\\\emph{squared} norm, which holds only when $\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P} \\\\\\\\leq 1/2$, and consequently carries the term $\\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P}$ into an overlap bound of $1 - 2\\\\\\\\delta_P - \\\\\\\\sqrt{\\\\\\\\delta_P}$. The proof above uses the corrected bound $4\\\\\\\\delta_P$, which gives the overlap bound $1 - 4\\\\\\\\delta_P$ and leaves the final bound $\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{qld}} = O(\\\\\\\\delta_P^{1/4} + md/q)$ unchanged. The source proof also normalizes the vector $(\\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\\\\\\\\ot M})_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{A}''\\\\\\\\mathrm{B}''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\vartheta}$ without ensuring that it is nonzero; the case distinction on $\\\\\\\\delta_P$ in the proof above supplies this, the conclusions of the lemma being trivial when $\\\\\\\\delta_P$ exceeds a universal constant.\\\\n   434\\\\t\\\\tThe numerical corrections and their role in the extraction argument are\\\\n   435\\\\t\\\\tdocumented in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_extraction-transfer}.\\\\n   436\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{remark}\\\\n   437\\\\t\\\\n   438\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Proof of the soundness of the Pauli basis test}\\\\n   439\\\\t\\\\n   440\\\\tWe can now prove the soundness theorem for the Pauli basis test, stated as Theorem~\\\\\\\\ref{thm:pauli} in Chapter~\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-test}.\\\\n   441\\\\t\\\\n   442\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{proof}\\\\n   443\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\proves{thm:pauli}\\\\n   444\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{lem:qld-unitary, lem:qld-extraction-error-form, lem:pauli-completeness,\\\\n   445\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tthm:naimark, lem:projective-strategy-setup, def:expanded-state,\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\nresults/telem