\t  simp [decodeAt, lowDegreeEnc_cubeEmbed, ha y]\\\\n   103\\\\t\\\\n   104\\\\tend MIPStarRE.QPBT\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"failed\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-364-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_186\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'git diff --name-status e2882e214927b7799f183cd25dbde489ae2e0e76..7316ed0d906b8bef274d9e3f9009e0f87ecf8793\\\\ngit diff --stat e2882e214927b7799f183cd25dbde489ae2e0e76..7316ed0d906b8bef274d9e3f9009e0f87ecf8793'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-365-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_186\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc 'git diff --name-status e2882e214927b7799f183cd25dbde489ae2e0e76..7316ed0d906b8bef274d9e3f9009e0f87ecf8793\\\\ngit diff --stat e2882e214927b7799f183cd25dbde489ae2e0e76..7316ed0d906b8bef274d9e3f9009e0f87ecf8793'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"M\\\\tblueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex\\\\nM\\\\tblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex\\\\nM\\\\tblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex\\\\nM\\\\tblueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex\\\\nM\\\\tblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex\\\\nM\\\\tblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex\\\\nM\\\\tblueprint/src/references.bib\\\\nA\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt-gap-register.md\\\\nA\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_anticommuting-probability.tex\\\\nM\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_characteristic-two-pauli-scope.tex\\\\nM\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex\\\\nM\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_delta-bound-exponent-comparison.tex\\\\nM\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_extraction-transfer.tex\\\\nM\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-sandwich-indexing.tex\\\\nM\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_linearity-theorem-quotation.tex\\\\nA\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_pauli-binary-factor-index.tex\\\\nM\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex\\\\nA\\\\tdocs/paper-gaps/qpbt_win-implications-corrections.tex\\\\n blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex        |  76 ++++++-----\\\\n blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex          |   2 +-\\\\n blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex           |   2 +-\\\\n blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex    |  20 +--\\\\n blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex      |  93 ++++++++++++--\\\\n blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex     |  69 +++++++++-\\\\n blueprint/src/references.bib                       | 109 ++++++++++++++++\\\\n docs/paper-gaps/qpbt-gap-register.md               |  45 +++++++\\\\n docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_anticommuting-probability.tex | 139 +++++++++++++++++++++\\\\n .../qpbt_characteristic-two-pauli-scope.tex        |  31 +++--\\\\n docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex |  88 ++++++++-----\\\\n .../qpbt_delta-bound-exponent-comparison.tex       |   3 +-\\\\n docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_extraction-transfer.tex       |  36 ++++--\\\\n docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-sandwich-indexing.tex      |   6 +-\\\\n .../qpbt_linearity-theorem-quotation.tex           |  58 ++++++---\\\\n docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_pauli-binary-factor-index.tex |  90 +++++++++++++\\\\n docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex |  62 +++++----\\\\n .../qpbt_win-implications-corrections.tex          | 133 ++++++++++++++++++++\\\\n 18 files changed, 909 insertions(+), 153 deletions(-)\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-366-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_187\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex | sed -n '1,280p'\\\\nnl -ba docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_win-implications-corrections.tex | sed -n '1,240p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-367-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_187\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_symmetrization-attainment.tex | sed -n '1,280p'\\\\nnl -ba docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_win-implications-corrections.tex | sed -n '1,240p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t\\\\\\\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t\\\\\\\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\\\\n     4\\\\t\\\\\\\\usepackage{xurl}\\\\n     5\\\\t\\\\\\\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\\\\n     6\\\\t\\\\\\\\setlength{\\\\\\\\emergencystretch}{2em}\\\\n     7\\\\t\\\\n     8\\\\t\\\\\\\\input{command}\\\\n     9\\\\t\\\\n    10\\\\t% Local notation matching the source paper (its style file is not shared here).\\\\n    11\\\\t\\\\\\\\newcommand{\\\\\\\\val}{\\\\\\\\operatorname{val}}\\\\n    12\\\\t\\\\\\\\newcommand{\\\\\\\\game}{\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}}\\\\n    13\\\\t\\\\\\\\newcommand{\\\\\\\\strategy}{\\\\\\\\mathcal{S}}\\\\n    14\\\\t\\\\\\\\renewcommand{\\\\\\\\ghissue}[1]{%\\\\n    15\\\\t  \\\\\\\\href{https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/issues/#1}{GitHub issue \\\\\\\\##1}}\\\\n    16\\\\t\\\\n    17\\\\t\\\\\\\\title{Attainment in the Symmetrization Lemma}\\\\n    18\\\\t\\\\\\\\author{}\\\\n    19\\\\t\\\\\\\\date{2026-08-30}\\\\n    20\\\\t\\\\n    21\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{document}\\\\n    22\\\\t\\\\\\\\maketitle\\\\n    23\\\\t\\\\n    24\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{At a glance}\\\\n    25\\\\t\\\\n    26\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{itemize}\\\\n    27\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Difficulty: easy.}  The issue is a quantifier exchange between\\\\n    28\\\\t  a supremum and an attained maximum in a preliminary lemma on nonlocal games.\\\\n    29\\\\t  No analytic estimate is missing; the substance is deciding which statement\\\\n    30\\\\t  the symmetrization proof supports and which statement the later arguments\\\\n    31\\\\t  consume.\\\\n    32\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Estimated weight:} about \\\\\\\\textbf{1--2 lemma interfaces} and on\\\\n    33\\\\t  the order of \\\\\\\\textbf{100--300 lines} of formal proof for the value-preserving\\\\n    34\\\\t  symmetrization construction.  The attainment step itself should not be\\\\n    35\\\\t  formalized as printed (see the Conclusion).\\\\n    36\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Mathlib/project split:} approximately \\\\\\\\textbf{20\\\\\\\\% Mathlib}\\\\n    37\\\\t  (finite-dimensional inner product spaces, tensor products, block\\\\n    38\\\\t  decompositions of $\\\\\\\\C^2 \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\C^d$) and \\\\\\\\textbf{80\\\\\\\\% project-local} (games,\\\\n    39\\\\t  strategies, values, and the Naimark input).\\\\n    40\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Key mathematical inputs:} the completed projective form of\\\\n    41\\\\t  Naimark dilation, \\\\\\\\cite[Theorem~5.1]{Ji2020LowIndividualDegree}, and the\\\\n    42\\\\t  definitions of symmetric games and tensor product values in the source\\\\n    43\\\\t  \\\\\\\\cite[Section~5]{Ji2020MIPStar}.  The note is audited against the\\\\n    44\\\\t  proof-gap protocol in \\\\\\\\ghissue{173}.\\\\n    45\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{itemize}\\\\n    46\\\\t\\\\n    47\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Key theorem forms}\\\\n    48\\\\t\\\\n    49\\\\tThree statements must be kept apart.  Throughout, $\\\\\\\\game$ denotes a symmetric\\\\n    50\\\\ttwo-player one-round game and $\\\\\\\\eps \\\\\\\\ge 0$ a real parameter; the notation is\\\\n    51\\\\tintroduced in the next section.\\\\n    52\\\\t\\\\n    53\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{enumerate}\\\\n    54\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Source form (attainment form).}  If\\\\n    55\\\\t  $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game) = 1-\\\\\\\\eps$, then there exists a symmetric and projective\\\\n    56\\\\t  strategy $\\\\\\\\strategy$ with $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy) \\\\\\\\ge 1-\\\\\\\\eps$.\\\\n    57\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Approximate form (what the source proof establishes).}  If\\\\n    58\\\\t  $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game) = 1-\\\\\\\\eps$, then for every $\\\\\\\\eps' > \\\\\\\\eps$ there exists a\\\\n    59\\\\t  symmetric and projective strategy $\\\\\\\\strategy$ with\\\\n    60\\\\t  $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy) \\\\\\\\ge 1-\\\\\\\\eps'$.\\\\n    61\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Given-strategy form (value-preserving symmetrization).}  If\\\\n    62\\\\t  $\\\\\\\\strategy'$ is any strategy for $\\\\\\\\game$ with\\\\n    63\\\\t  $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy') \\\\\\\\ge 1-\\\\\\\\eps$, then there exists a symmetric and\\\\n    64\\\\t  projective strategy $\\\\\\\\strategy$ with\\\\n    65\\\\t  $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy) = \\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy') \\\\\\\\ge 1-\\\\\\\\eps$.\\\\n    66\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{enumerate}\\\\n    67\\\\t\\\\n    68\\\\tThe source proof consists exactly of a proof of the third form, applied to a\\\\n    69\\\\tstrategy supplied by the definition of the supremum; this yields the second\\\\n    70\\\\tform.  The first form asserts strictly more than the second, and the passage\\\\n    71\\\\tfrom the second to the first is the gap discussed in this note.  Every use of\\\\n    72\\\\tthe lemma, in the source and in this project, consumes only the second or the\\\\n    73\\\\tthird form.\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{The source assertion}\\\\n    76\\\\t\\\\n    77\\\\tA two-player one-round game\\\\n    78\\\\t$\\\\\\\\game = (\\\\\\\\mathcal X, \\\\\\\\mathcal A, \\\\\\\\mu, D)$ in compact symmetric notation\\\\n    79\\\\tconsists of a finite question alphabet $\\\\\\\\mathcal X$, a finite answer alphabet\\\\n    80\\\\t$\\\\\\\\mathcal A$, a symmetric question distribution $\\\\\\\\mu$ on\\\\n    81\\\\t$\\\\\\\\mathcal X \\\\\\\\times \\\\\\\\mathcal X$, and a decision predicate $D$ treating the two\\\\n    82\\\\tplayers symmetrically.  A tensor product strategy\\\\n    83\\\\t$\\\\\\\\strategy = (\\\\\\\\ket\\\\\\\\psi, A, B)$ consists of a unit vector $\\\\\\\\ket\\\\\\\\psi$ in a\\\\n    84\\\\ttensor product $\\\\\\\\mathcal H_A \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\mathcal H_B$ of \\\\\\\\emph{finite-dimensional}\\\\n    85\\\\tHilbert spaces together with POVMs $\\\\\\\\{A^x_a\\\\\\\\}$ and $\\\\\\\\{B^x_a\\\\\\\\}$ for the two\\\\n    86\\\\tplayers; its value $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy)$ is the acceptance probability,\\\\n    87\\\\tand the value of the game is the supremum\\\\n    88\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{equation*}\\\\n    89\\\\t  \\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game) = \\\\\\\\sup_{\\\\\\\\strategy} \\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy)\\\\n    90\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{equation*}\\\\n    91\\\\tover all tensor product strategies.  A strategy is projective if all its\\\\n    92\\\\tmeasurements are projective, and symmetric if the state is\\\\n    93\\\\tpermutation-invariant on $\\\\\\\\mathcal H \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\mathcal H$ and both players use the\\\\n    94\\\\tsame measurements.\\\\n    95\\\\t\\\\n    96\\\\tThe symmetrization lemma of \\\\\\\\cite[Section~5]{Ji2020MIPStar} asserts:%\\\\n    97\\\\t\\\\\\\\footnote{The statement is at\\\\n    98\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex}, lines~94--99,\\\\n    99\\\\tand its proof at lines~101--132.  The blueprint statement kept in this form\\\\n   100\\\\tis \\\\\\\\path{lem:symmetric-strat} in\\\\n   101\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex}.}\\\\n   102\\\\tif $\\\\\\\\game$ is a symmetric game with $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game) = 1-\\\\\\\\eps$ for some\\\\n   103\\\\t$\\\\\\\\eps \\\\\\\\ge 0$, then\\\\n   104\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{equation*}\\\\n   105\\\\t  \\\\\\\\exists\\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\strategy = (\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\psi}, M) \\\\\\\\text{ symmetric and projective}\\\\n   106\\\\t  \\\\\\\\quad\\\\\\\\text{with}\\\\\\\\quad\\\\n   107\\\\t  \\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy) \\\\\\\\ge 1-\\\\\\\\eps.\\\\n   108\\\\t  \\\\\\\\tag{\\\\\\\\path{lem:symmetric-strat}}\\\\n   109\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{equation*}\\\\n   110\\\\t\\\\n   111\\\\tIts proof runs as follows.  For every $\\\\\\\\eps' > \\\\\\\\eps$ the definition of the\\\\n   112\\\\tsupremum supplies a strategy $\\\\\\\\strategy' = (\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\psi'}, A, B)$ with\\\\n   113\\\\t$\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy') \\\\\\\\ge 1-\\\\\\\\eps'$.  By Naimark dilation in the completed\\\\n   114\\\\tprojective form of \\\\\\\\cite[Theorem~5.1]{Ji2020LowIndividualDegree} one may take\\\\n   115\\\\t$\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\psi'} \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\C^d_{A'} \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\C^d_{B'}$ for some integer $d$ with all\\\\n   116\\\\tmeasurements projective.  One then forms the permutation-invariant state\\\\n   117\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{equation*}\\\\n   118\\\\t  \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\psi} = \\\\\\\\tfrac{1}{\\\\\\\\sqrt 2}\\\\n   119\\\\t  \\\\\\\\bigl( \\\\\\\\ket{0}_A \\\\\\\\ket{1}_B \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\psi'}_{A'B'}\\\\n   120\\\\t       + \\\\\\\\ket{1}_A \\\\\\\\ket{0}_B \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\psi'_\\\\\\\\tau}_{A'B'} \\\\\\\\bigr)\\\\n   121\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{equation*}\\\\n   122\\\\ton $(\\\\\\\\C^2 \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\C^d) \\\\\\\\ot (\\\\\\\\C^2 \\\\\\\\ot \\\\\\\\C^d)$, where $\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\psi'_\\\\\\\\tau}$ permutes\\\\n   123\\\\tthe two players' registers, and the block-diagonal projective measurements\\\\n   124\\\\t$M^x_a = \\\\\\\\ket{0}\\\\\\\\!\\\\\\\\bra{0} \\\\\\\\ot A^x_a + \\\\\\\\ket{1}\\\\\\\\!\\\\\\\\bra{1} \\\\\\\\ot B^x_a$.  Symmetry\\\\n   125\\\\tof $D$ gives $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, (\\\\\\\\ket\\\\\\\\psi, M)) = \\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game, \\\\\\\\strategy')$.  The\\\\n   126\\\\tconstruction is therefore \\\\\\\\emph{value-preserving}: applied to any strategy it\\\\n   127\\\\tproduces a symmetric projective strategy of exactly the same value.  What the\\\\n   128\\\\tproof establishes is thus the given-strategy form, hence the approximate form;\\\\n   129\\\\tthe printed conclusion is the attainment form.\\\\n   130\\\\t\\\\n   131\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Why attainment does not follow}\\\\n   132\\\\t\\\\n   133\\\\tThe supremum defining $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game)$ ranges over strategies on\\\\n   134\\\\tfinite-dimensional Hilbert spaces of unbounded dimension.  The strategies\\\\n   135\\\\t$\\\\\\\\strategy'_{\\\\\\\\eps'}$ produced for $\\\\\\\\eps' \\\\\\\\downarrow \\\\\\\\eps$ may require\\\\n   136\\\\tdimensions $d(\\\\\\\\eps')$ growing without bound, and there is no compactness\\\\n   137\\\\tacross dimensions from which a limiting finite-dimensional strategy of value\\\\n   138\\\\tat least $1-\\\\\\\\eps$ could be extracted.  A symmetric projective strategy of\\\\n   139\\\\tvalue at least $1-\\\\\\\\eps = \\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game)$ would attain the supremum, so the\\\\n   140\\\\tprinted conclusion is equivalent, under its hypothesis, to the assertion that\\\\n   141\\\\t$\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game)$ is attained by some strategy.  No general principle supplies\\\\n   142\\\\tthis: it is known, and recalled in the introduction of the source itself, that\\\\n   143\\\\tthe set of finite-dimensional quantum correlations is not closed and differs\\\\n   144\\\\tfrom the set of infinite-dimensional spatial correlations, so limits of\\\\n   145\\\\tfinite-dimensional strategies need not be realized by any finite-dimensional\\\\n   146\\\\tstrategy.  Whether some symmetric game realizes the failure --- a game whose\\\\n   147\\\\tvalue is attained by no tensor product strategy, presented together with the\\\\n   148\\\\texposing functional as a decision predicate --- is a separate question that\\\\n   149\\\\tthis note does not need to settle.  The local verdict is about the proof: the\\\\n   150\\\\tcited argument proves the approximate form and does not prove the attainment\\\\n   151\\\\tform.\\\\n   152\\\\t\\\\n   153\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Uses of the lemma}\\\\n   154\\\\t\\\\n   155\\\\tThe source invokes the lemma twice.\\\\n   156\\\\t\\\\n   157\\\\tFirst, in the soundness proof for the oracularization transformation, the\\\\n   158\\\\targument fixes a strategy $\\\\\\\\strategy^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{orac}}$ for the oracularized game\\\\n   159\\\\t``with value $1-\\\\\\\\eps$'' and applies the lemma to assume without loss of\\\\n   160\\\\tgenerality that it is projective.%\\\\n   161\\\\t\\\\\\\\footnote{\\\\\\\\path{references/qpbt-paper/10_oracularization.tex},\\\\n   162\\\\tlines~317--321.}\\\\n   163\\\\tHere the input is a given strategy, not the value of the game; the\\\\n   164\\\\tgiven-strategy form applies verbatim and preserves the value exactly, so the\\\\n   165\\\\tuse is justified by what the proof establishes.\\\\n   166\\\\t\\\\n   167\\\\tSecond, in the soundness proof for answer reduction, the argument assumes the\\\\n   168\\\\tstrict inequality $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game) > 1-\\\\\\\\eps$ and concludes that there is a\\\\n   169\\\\tsymmetric projective strategy of value greater than $1-\\\\\\\\eps$.%\\\\n   170\\\\t\\\\\\\\footnote{\\\\\\\\path{references/qpbt-paper/11_answer_reduction.tex},\\\\n   171\\\\tlines~2322--2332.}\\\\n   172\\\\tWriting $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game) = 1-\\\\\\\\eps_0$ with $\\\\\\\\eps_0 < \\\\\\\\eps$ and applying the\\\\n   173\\\\tapproximate form with $\\\\\\\\eps' = (\\\\\\\\eps+\\\\\\\\eps_0)/2$ produces a symmetric\\\\n   174\\\\tprojective strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\eps' > 1-\\\\\\\\eps$.  A strict lower\\\\n   175\\\\tbound on the supremum thus passes through the approximate form; attainment is\\\\n   176\\\\tnot used.\\\\n   177\\\\t\\\\n   178\\\\tIn this project, the soundness statements of the Pauli basis test track\\\\n   179\\\\tquantify over strategies assumed to succeed with probability at least\\\\n   180\\\\t$1-\\\\\\\\eps$, so any symmetrization step starts from a given strategy and consumes\\\\n   181\\\\tthe given-strategy form.  The blueprint records both forms as part of the\\\\n   182\\\\tgames vocabulary and has no downstream dependency on either; the two source\\\\n   183\\\\tuses above belong to transformations outside the scope of the present\\\\n   184\\\\tdevelopment.\\\\n   185\\\\tConsequently, no consumer of the lemma --- in the source or here --- requires\\\\n   186\\\\tthe attainment form.\\\\n   187\\\\t\\\\n   188\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Comparison with the blueprint}\\\\n   189\\\\t\\\\n   190\\\\tThe blueprint \\\\\\\\cite{MIPStarREBlueprint} states the lemma in the source shape,\\\\n   191\\\\tas the proof-gap protocol requires when the printed statement is not known to\\\\n   192\\\\tbe false and only its proof is blocked.  Its proof records the\\\\n   193\\\\tvalue-preserving construction and the approximate form that the construction\\\\n   194\\\\tyields, and explicitly marks the remaining attainment step as unproved, citing\\\\n   195\\\\tthis note; an accompanying remark summarizes the obstruction.  The\\\\n   196\\\\tvalue-preserving given-strategy form is stated beside it as a separate\\\\n   197\\\\tformalization-support node, \\\\\\\\path{lem:symmetric-strat-given-strategy}, which\\\\n   198\\\\tis not advertised as the source lemma.\\\\n   199\\\\t\\\\n   200\\\\tThe two Lean declarations follow the same separation.  The source-shaped\\\\n   201\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanid{exists\\\\\\\\_symmetric\\\\\\\\_projective\\\\\\\\_strategy} is linked to\\\\n   202\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{lem:symmetric-strat}; its proof is the tracked attainment obligation and\\\\n   203\\\\tremains open.  The given-strategy\\\\n   204\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanid{exists\\\\\\\\_symmetric\\\\\\\\_projective\\\\\\\\_strategy\\\\\\\\_of\\\\\\\\_strategy}, linked to the\\\\n   205\\\\tsupport node, has the same hypothesis, exact value equality, and projective\\\\n   206\\\\tsymmetric conclusion as that node, and its proof is complete.\\\\n   207\\\\t\\\\n   208\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Conclusion}\\\\n   209\\\\t\\\\n   210\\\\tThe verdict is a proof-level gap in the cited lemma: the symmetrization\\\\n   211\\\\targument proves the given-strategy and approximate forms, while the printed\\\\n   212\\\\tconclusion additionally asserts that the supremum defining $\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\game)$ is\\\\n   213\\\\tattained, which does not follow.  The gap is harmless for the results built\\\\n   214\\\\ton the lemma, since both uses in the source, and all planned uses in this\\\\n   215\\\\tproject, proceed from a given strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\eps$ or from a\\\\n   216\\\\tstrict lower bound on the value, for which the value-preserving construction\\\\n   217\\\\tsuffices.  Stage~4 has carried out the recommendation of this note: the\\\\n   218\\\\tgiven-strategy symmetrization lemma is formalized and proved as the workhorse\\\\n   219\\\\tstatement, while the source-labelled lemma keeps its source shape with the\\\\n   220\\\\tattainment step an explicit, tracked proof obligation.  If a later\\\\n   221\\\\tinvestigation settles the counterexample question for symmetric games, the\\\\n   222\\\\tstatement should then be reclassified from an unproved step to a documented\\\\n   223\\\\tstatement correction.\\\\n   224\\\\t\\\\n   225\\\\t\\\\\\\\bibliographystyle{alpha}\\\\n   226\\\\t\\\\\\\\bibliography{references}\\\\n   227\\\\t\\\\n   228\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{document}\\\\n     1\\\\t\\\\\\\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\\\\n     2\\\\t\\\\n     3\\\\t\\\\\\\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\\\\n     4\\\\t\\\\\\\\usepackage{xurl}\\\\n     5\\\\t\\\\\\\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\\\\n     6\\\\t\\\\\\\\setlength{\\\\\\\\emergencystretch}{2em}\\\\n     7\\\\t\\\\n     8\\\\t\\\\\\\\input{command}\\\\n     9\\\\t\\\\n    10\\\\t\\\\\\\\newcommand{\\\\\\\\ind}{\\\\\\\\operatorname{ind}}\\\\n    11\\\\t\\\\\\\\renewcommand{\\\\\\\\ghissue}[1]{%\\\\n    12\\\\t  \\\\\\\\href{https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/issues/#1}{GitHub issue \\\\\\\\##1}}\\\\n    13\\\\t\\\\n    14\\\\t\\\\\\\\title{Corrections to the Pauli-Test Winning Implications}\\\\n    15\\\\t\\\\\\\\author{}\\\\n    16\\\\t\\\\\\\\date{2026-09-04}\\\\n    17\\\\t\\\\n    18\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{document}\\\\n    19\\\\t\\\\\\\\maketitle\\\\n    20\\\\t\\\\n    21\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{At a glance}\\\\n    22\\\\t\\\\n    23\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{itemize}\\\\n    24\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Difficulty.} Low to medium.  The subtest implications are\\\\n    25\\\\t  direct after conditioning, but the printed proof uses an invalid parameter\\\\n    26\\\\t  reduction and two displayed formulas contain wrong indices.\\\\n    27\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Estimated weight.} The formal work is the family of exact and\\\\n    28\\\\t  approximate winning implications, roughly 300--500 lines after the sampling\\\\n    29\\\\t  probability results are available.\\\\n    30\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Mathlib/project split.} About 20\\\\\\\\% finite-probability\\\\n    31\\\\t  bookkeeping and 80\\\\\\\\% project-local game predicates, post-processing, and\\\\n    32\\\\t  state-dependent distance transfer.\\\\n    33\\\\t  \\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\textbf{Key mathematical inputs.} Constant lower bounds for the\\\\n    34\\\\t  commuting and anticommuting events, data processing, and the one-way Magic\\\\n    35\\\\t  Square rigidity theorem.  The proof packets are \\\\\\\\ghissue{112} and\\\\n    36\\\\t  \\\\\\\\ghissue{113}.\\\\n    37\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{itemize}\\\\n    38\\\\t\\\\n    39\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Key theorem forms}\\\\n    40\\\\t\\\\n    41\\\\tFor an admissible tuple $(q,m,d)$ and a strategy that wins the Pauli basis test\\\\n    42\\\\twith probability at least $1-\\\\\\\\eps$, each subtest has conditional failure\\\\n    43\\\\t$O(\\\\\\\\eps)$.  In particular, the Magic Square average is conditioned on\\\\n    44\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n    45\\\\t  \\\\\\\\gamma(\\\\\\\\omega)\\\\n    46\\\\t  =\\\\\\\\tr\\\\\\\\big((r_X\\\\\\\\ind_m(u_X))\\\\\\\\cdot(r_Z\\\\\\\\ind_m(u_Z))\\\\\\\\big)\\\\\\\\ne0,\\\\n    47\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n    48\\\\tand the low-degree line-evaluation family is completed on zero-direction lines\\\\n    49\\\\tby an additional outcome.  The observable consequence is\\\\n    50\\\\t\\\\\\\\[\\\\n    51\\\\t  X^{r_X}(u_X)Z^{r_Z}(u_Z)\\\\n    52\\\\t  \\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\sqrt\\\\\\\\eps}\\\\n    53\\\\t  (-1)^{\\\\\\\\gamma(\\\\\\\\omega)}Z^{r_Z}(u_Z)X^{r_X}(u_X)\\\\n    54\\\\t\\\\\\\\]\\\\n    55\\\\ton average over all tuples.  These statements hold for every admissible\\\\n    56\\\\tparameter tuple; no assumption $6md\\\\\\\\leq q$ is needed.\\\\n    57\\\\t\\\\n    58\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{The source assertions and discrepancies}\\\\n    59\\\\t\\\\n    60\\\\tThe source states the measurement implications at lines~197--265 and the\\\\n    61\\\\tobservable implications at lines~267--362 of the Pauli analysis\\\\n    62\\\\t\\\\\\\\cite[lines~197--362]{Ji2020MIPStar}.%\\\\n    63\\\\t\\\\\\\\footnote{See\\\\n    64\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex}.}\\\\n    65\\\\tFour corrections are required.\\\\n    66\\\\t\\\\n    67\\\\tFirst, the displayed conditioning event for the Magic Square average omits\\\\n    68\\\\t$\\\\\\\\ind_m$ and writes the scalar expression\\\\n    69\\\\t$\\\\\\\\tr((r_Xu_X)\\\\\\\\cdot(r_Zu_Z))$, even though $u_X,u_Z\\\\\\\\in\\\\\\\\F_q^m$ and the phase\\\\n    70\\\\tused by the game is defined through vectors in $\\\\\\\\F_q^{2^m}$.\\\\n    71\\\\t\\\\n    72\\\\tSecond, the proof assumes $6md\\\\\\\\leq q$ and disposes of the complementary range\\\\n    73\\\\tby appealing to the final Pauli soundness theorem, whose proof uses the lemma\\\\n    74\\\\tunder discussion.  That appeal cannot prove the lemma as an unrestricted\\\\n    75\\\\tstandalone result.  The corrected exact probability calculation gives\\\\n    76\\\\tuniversal lower bounds for both conditioning events whenever the parameters\\\\n    77\\\\tare admissible, and removes this circular reduction.%\\\\n    78\\\\t\\\\\\\\footnote{The probability correction is documented separately in\\\\n    79\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_anticommuting-probability.tex}.}\\\\n    80\\\\t\\\\n    81\\\\tThird, the source treats evaluation classes of a line measurement as a POVM\\\\n    82\\\\tindexed by $\\\\\\\\F_q$.  A zero-direction line admits nonconstant polynomial\\\\n    83\\\\trepresentatives with no well-defined value on its singleton image, so these\\\\n    84\\\\tclasses form only a sub-measurement.  Adding an outcome $\\\\\\\\bot$ for the missing\\\\n    85\\\\tmass makes the consistency relation well typed; the point family is completed\\\\n    86\\\\tby a zero effect at the same outcome.\\\\n    87\\\\t\\\\n    88\\\\tFinally, the observable proof writes\\\\n    89\\\\t$Z^{r_X}(u_X)X^{r_Z}(u_Z)$ where the intended reversed product is\\\\n    90\\\\t$Z^{r_Z}(u_Z)X^{r_X}(u_X)$.  The source label prefix\\\\n    91\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{len:qld-win-implications-obs} is likewise a typographical error for\\\\n    92\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{lem:qld-win-implications-obs}.\\\\n    93\\\\t\\\\n    94\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{The corrected argument}\\\\n    95\\\\t\\\\n    96\\\\tEvery question type and every relevant subtest has a universal positive\\\\n    97\\\\tsampling weight.  For admissible parameters, $1\\\\\\\\leq m\\\\\\\\leq q$, and the exact\\\\n    98\\\\tcalculation of the anticommuting probability gives probability at least\\\\n    99\\\\t$2^{-4}$ for the anticommuting event and at least $1/2$ for its complement.\\\\n   100\\\\tConditioning therefore enlarges rejection probabilities only by a universal\\\\n   101\\\\tfactor.  The measurement implications follow directly from their rejection\\\\n   102\\\\tevents, including the completed zero-direction outcome.  Data processing and\\\\n   103\\\\tthe agreement identities yield the observable relations; the corrected Magic\\\\n   104\\\\tSquare phase and reversed product then give the displayed signed commutation\\\\n   105\\\\tlaw.\\\\n   106\\\\t\\\\n   107\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Blueprint and formalization status}\\\\n   108\\\\t\\\\n   109\\\\tThe blueprint uses the full phase $\\\\\\\\gamma$, completes the line-evaluation\\\\n   110\\\\tfamilies, proves the conditioning step with the universal probability bounds,\\\\n   111\\\\tand corrects the reversed product and label.  Its proof and correction remark\\\\n   112\\\\tcite this note.  The linked formal declarations use the same conditional\\\\n   113\\\\tdistributions and completed line outcomes, so their statements agree with the\\\\n   114\\\\tcorrected blueprint.  Their proofs remain open in the current tree.%\\\\n   115\\\\t\\\\\\\\footnote{The relevant declarations are \\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\_cons},\\\\n   116\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\_low\\\\\\\\_degree}, \\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\_pauli\\\\\\\\_basis\\\\\\\\_cons},\\\\n   117\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\_comm}, \\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\_comm\\\\\\\\_cons},\\\\n   118\\\\t\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\_magic\\\\\\\\_square}, \\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\_ms\\\\\\\\_cons}, and their\\\\n   119\\\\t\\\\\\\\path{\\\\\\\\_approx} companions in\\\\n   120\\\\t\\\\\\\\doclink{MIPStarRE/QPBT/Observables/WinImplications.lean}.}\\\\n   121\\\\t\\\\n   122\\\\t\\\\\\\\section{Conclusion}\\\\n   123\\\\t\\\\n   124\\\\tThe winning implications remain valid for all admissible parameters, but the\\\\n   125\\\\tprinted proof does not establish that scope and several formulas need local\\\\n   126\\\\tcorrection.  Exact conditioning probabilities, the explicit missing outcome,\\\\n   127\\\\tand the corrected phase and operator indices give the form used by the Pauli\\\\n   128\\\\tbasis analysis.\\\\n   129\\\\t\\\\n   130\\\\t\\\\\\\\bibliographystyle{alpha}\\\\n   131\\\\t\\\\\\\\bibliography{references}\\\\n   132\\\\t\\\\n   133\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{document}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-368-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_188\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(consum(e|es|ed|er|ers|ing)|provider(-side)?|downstream|upstream|formalized|formalization mark|linked declaration|Lean declaration|proof-level mark|statement-level mark|support node|workhorse)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl:369:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_188\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(consum(e|es|ed|er|ers|ing)|provider(-side)?|downstream|upstream|formalized|formalization mark|linked declaration|Lean declaration|proof-level mark|statement-level mark|support node|workhorse)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:389:\\\\tNo Lean declaration states this lemma. The only existence declaration available assumes the global polynomial-pair measurement of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7} as data, instead of obtaining it from that lemma as the proof below does; it is therefore a conditional helper, it does not certify the statement above, and it is not linked here. It is recorded instead in the formalization-support node Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary-given-global-pair} below, as the proof-gap protocol requires. The discrepancy and the source-facing declaration that must replace it are recorded in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_extraction-transfer}.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:399:% This support node records a conditional Lean helper; it is not a statement\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:407:\\\\tThe statement-level mark records that the linked declaration has exactly this shape, assumed measurement included; it does not certify Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary}, whose proof obtains that measurement from Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7}. By the criterion of the proof-gap protocol the assumed measurement is proof debt rather than a faithful boundary hypothesis. The source-facing declaration that must replace it, and the correction of the linked declaration's name and docstring, which still describe it as source-facing, are recorded in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_extraction-transfer}.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:411:\\\\tThe proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-unitary} above, with its appeal to Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-7} replaced by the assumed measurement. The proof of the linked declaration is open, so no proof-level mark is placed here.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:786:\\\\tThe formalized proof is a relabelling argument rather than a factorwise\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:814:\\\\tLemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:pauli-observable-expansion} is formalized; its\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:815:\\\\tgeneral-prime expansion and inversion have no Lean declaration, as\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:816:\\\\trecorded in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_characteristic-two-pauli-scope}. The formalized\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:84:% rem:linearity-distance-normalization. The provider imposes no upper bound\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:92:% extension via its ampliation S ot Id. The provider prints the closeness\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:272:\\\\tprovider-side correction to $2\\\\\\\\delta$ is carried by\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:280:\\\\t\\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_linearity-theorem-quotation}, and the provider-side\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1765:\\\\t$m \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\poly(\\\\\\\\eps, md/q)$, which is the form consumed by\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1787:\\\\tLemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}, and no formalization mark is placed on the\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1788:\\\\tstatement: the linked declaration differs from it in three further\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:137:\\\\tThe proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:symmetric-strat} yields, for each $\\\\\\\\eps' > \\\\\\\\eps$, a symmetric projective strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\eps'$. The conclusion as stated, at $\\\\\\\\eps' = \\\\\\\\eps$, does not follow from this: the dilated dimension $d$ may grow as $\\\\\\\\eps' \\\\\\\\downarrow \\\\\\\\eps$, and the supremum defining $\\\\\\\\operatorname{val}^*(\\\\\\\\mathfrak G)$ in Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:tensor-product-value} need not be attained by any strategy. The symmetrization construction itself is value-preserving, so the conclusion does hold whenever the hypothesis supplies an actual strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\eps$ rather than only the value of the game; every use of the lemma in the source proceeds from such a strategy, or from a strict lower bound on the value, and therefore consumes only what the proof establishes. The gap and the available repairs are documented in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_symmetrization-attainment}.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:279:\\\\t% Status: the statement is final; no Lean declaration exists yet for the full disjunctive form, so this node carries no formalization marker.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:1359:\\\\tLet $\\\\\\\\mathcal T$ be a set (the \\\\\\\\emph{type set}) and let $V$ be $\\\\\\\\F^n$ for some integer $n \\\\\\\\ge 0$. A \\\\\\\\emph{$\\\\\\\\mathcal T$-typed family of $\\\\\\\\ell$-level conditionally linear functions} (implicitly, \\\\\\\\emph{on $V$}) is a collection $\\\\\\\\{L_t\\\\\\\\}_{t \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\mathcal T}$ such that, for each $t \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\mathcal T$, $L_t$ is an $\\\\\\\\ell$-level conditionally linear function on $V$. Finiteness of $\\\\\\\\mathcal T$ plays no part in this definition, which is therefore stated, as in the linked declaration, for an arbitrary type set; it is required from Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:graph-distribution} onwards, where $\\\\\\\\mathcal T$ indexes a distribution. The source states the definition for a finite type set, and every type set occurring below is finite.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:1394:% The Lean declaration typedCLDistribution is stated for arbitrary T-indexed families of maps\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:6:This chapter defines the two testing primitives underlying the question-reduction step: the \\\\\\\\emph{classical low individual degree game}, in its simultaneous form, and the \\\\\\\\emph{Pauli basis test}, a nonlocal game built from the classical game together with the Magic Square game. We state the quantum soundness of the classical game (Theorem~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-soundness}, imported, with the facts required by the identification, which remain to be proved, recorded in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}; see Remark~\\\\\\\\ref{rem:ld-soundness-provider}), the rigidity of the Magic Square game (Theorem~\\\\\\\\ref{thm:ms-rigidity}, imported), completeness of the Pauli basis test (Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:pauli-completeness}), and the main soundness theorem for the Pauli basis test (Theorem~\\\\\\\\ref{thm:pauli}), whose proof occupies Chapters~\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-observables}--\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-extraction} and is completed in Chapter~\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-extraction} only modulo the proof obligation documented in \\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}. The chapter closes with the qubit form of the soundness statement (Corollary~\\\\\\\\ref{cor:pauli-binary}) and the canonical parameter choice with its soundness bound (Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:introparams}, Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:delta-bound}).\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:87:\\\\t% No completion mark: the linked declaration proves the distribution identity only, not the typed-family assertion. See the last paragraph of the statement; the open family assertion is tracked by issue 180.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:89:\\\\tFix $\\\\\\\\mathsf{ldparams} = (q,m,d,k)$ as in Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:ld-game}, let $L = \\\\\\\\{L_t\\\\\\\\}_{t \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}}$ be the family of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}, and let $G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ be the graph on $\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ all of whose unordered pairs, self-loops included, are edges. Then the question distribution of $\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ is the $(\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}, G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}})$-typed conditionally linear distribution $\\\\\\\\mu^{G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}}_{L,\\\\\\\\,L}$ of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}. The linked declaration proves the distribution identity: the question distribution of $\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ equals the distribution that the construction of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions} produces from the pair $(L, L)$ and the graph $G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$, a construction that is available for an arbitrary family of maps. It does not prove that $L$ is a $\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$-typed family of conditionally linear functions of one common level, which is what makes the right-hand side a typed conditionally linear distribution in the sense of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}: Lemmas~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-aline-level} and~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-dline-level} give the levels of $L_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{ALine}}$ and $L_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{DLine}}$, while the level of $L_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{Point}}$ and the passage of the three maps to a common level are not formalized. That family assertion is open and is tracked as issue~\\\\\\\\#180, so the statement and the proof below carry no completion mark.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:232:\\\\tQuantum soundness of the low individual degree test itself is the result of~\\\\\\\\cite{Ji2020LowIndividualDegree}; Remark~\\\\\\\\ref{rem:ld-soundness-provider} relates the present statement to Theorem~\\\\\\\\ref{thm:main-formal}, which proves that result.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:235:\\\\\\\\begin{remark}[Relation to the low individual degree test of Chapter~\\\\\\\\ref{chap:test}]\\\\\\\\label{rem:ld-soundness-provider}\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:397:\\\\tFix an admissible tuple $\\\\\\\\mathsf{qldparams} = (q,m,d)$ (Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:admissible}) and let $L = \\\\\\\\{L_t\\\\\\\\}_{t \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}}$ be the family of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:pauli-question-distribution}. Then the question distribution of $\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli}}_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{qldparams}}$ is the $(\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}, G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}})$-typed conditionally linear distribution $\\\\\\\\mu^{G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}}_{L,\\\\\\\\,L}$ of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}. As in Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-question-typed-cl}, the linked declaration states the distribution identity alone: an equality between the question sampler of $\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli}}_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{qldparams}}$ and the distribution that the construction of Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions} produces from the pair $(L, L)$ and the graph $G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}$, a construction that is available for an arbitrary family of maps. Neither that equality nor the assertion that $L$ is a $\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}$-typed family of conditionally linear functions is formalized: the Lean proof of the equality is open, and so is the level assertion for the maps $L_t$ listed in Definition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:pauli-question-distribution}. Both obligations are tracked as issue~\\\\\\\\#180, so the statement and the proof below carry no completion mark.\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:401:\\\\tThe type pair is drawn from $\\\\\\\\mu_{G^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}}$ by definition, and for each ordered type pair the content pair is the image of a single uniform $z \\\\\\\\in V^{\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}$ under the corresponding pair of CL functions, that is, a sample from $\\\\\\\\mu_{L_{t_{\\\\\\\\mathrm A}},\\\\\\\\, L_{t_{\\\\\\\\mathrm B}}}$. This is the argument of the source; it is not yet formalized, and the typed-family hypotheses on $L$ are open as well.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-370-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_189\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Apply.lean | sed -n '1,150p'\\\\nnl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean | sed -n '250,325p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl:371:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_189\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Apply.lean | sed -n '1,150p'\\\\nnl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean | sed -n '250,325p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Points\\\\n     2\\\\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.SoundnessDefs\\\\n     3\\\\t\\\\n     4\\\\t/-!\\\\n     5\\\\t# Applying the classical low-degree test\\\\n     6\\\\t\\\\n     7\\\\tThis module states the two application obligations at the end of the Pauli-basis\\\\n     8\\\\tcombining argument.  The combined-line measurement is recorded both with the error\\\\n     9\\\\tform asserted by the source and with the weaker estimate established by its first\\\\n    10\\\\tproof route.  The final witness consists of a projective measurement of a pair of\\\\n    11\\\\tglobal bounded individual-degree polynomials.  The proposition-valued declarations\\\\n    12\\\\tbelow are intentionally open proof obligations in this skeleton; their statement\\\\n    13\\\\tlinks do not claim proof closure.\\\\n    14\\\\t\\\\n    15\\\\t## References\\\\n    16\\\\t\\\\n    17\\\\tThe combined-line declarations formalize `lem:qld-4-13` in\\\\n    18\\\\t`blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex`, with paper source\\\\n    19\\\\t`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020-1034`.\\\\n    20\\\\tThe global-pair declaration formalizes `lem:qld-4-7` in the same blueprint, with\\\\n    21\\\\tpaper source\\\\n    22\\\\t`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1267-1274`.\\\\n    23\\\\t-/\\\\n    24\\\\t\\\\n    25\\\\tnamespace MIPStarRE.QPBT\\\\n    26\\\\t\\\\n    27\\\\tnoncomputable section\\\\n    28\\\\t\\\\n    29\\\\t/-- Conditional construction of the extended-line measurements with the source error\\\\n    30\\\\t`poly(m^2 * epsilon, md / q)`.  This is the source-facing statement of\\\\n    31\\\\t`lem:qld-4-13`, paper lines 1020--1034.\\\\n    32\\\\t\\\\n    33\\\\tThe printed proof does not establish this error form: its first route gives\\\\n    34\\\\t`m * poly(epsilon, md / q)`, while its second route gives a different bound and\\\\n    35\\\\tuses a joint-law decomposition absent from the subline lemma.  The discrepancy is\\\\n    36\\\\tdocumented in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex` and\\\\n    37\\\\t`rem:qld-4-13-source-defects` in the blueprint.  The directly indexed line carrier\\\\n    38\\\\tused by `ExtendedLinesWitness` represents the required extended-dimensional\\\\n    39\\\\tline-point law without the invalid divisibility guard; it is a directly indexed\\\\n    40\\\\tline-space construction and does\\\\n    41\\\\tnot identify the source's seed-bearing verifier game with the directly indexed game.\\\\n    42\\\\tThis declaration takes an already constructed point witness; the\\\\n    43\\\\tsource-facing declaration below supplies that witness existentially.\\\\n    44\\\\t-/\\\\n    45\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness_ofPointsWitness :\\\\n    46\\\\t    ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\n    47\\\\t      ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε δQ : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε)\\\\n    48\\\\t        (points : CombinedPointsWitness S δQ),\\\\n    49\\\\t        Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\n    50\\\\t          (deltaCombine ((P.m : ℝ) ^ 2 * ε)\\\\n    51\\\\t            ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\n    52\\\\t  sorry\\\\n    53\\\\t\\\\n    54\\\\t/-! The source-facing declaration supplies the point witness from\\\\n    55\\\\t`lem:qld-4-10` rather than taking it as an unproved external hypothesis. -/\\\\n    56\\\\t\\\\n    57\\\\t/-- The source-facing extended-line construction of `lem:qld-4-13`, paper\\\\n    58\\\\tlines 1020--1034.\\\\n    59\\\\t\\\\n    60\\\\tThe `_ofPointsWitness` companion is the conditional, Lean-only form retained\\\\n    61\\\\tfor calculations that already have a point witness. -/\\\\n    62\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness :\\\\n    63\\\\t    ∃ deltaQ : ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr deltaQ ∧\\\\n    64\\\\t      ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\n    65\\\\t        ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε),\\\\n    66\\\\t          ∃ points : CombinedPointsWitness S (deltaQ ε),\\\\n    67\\\\t            Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\n    68\\\\t              (deltaCombine ((P.m : ℝ) ^ 2 * ε)\\\\n    69\\\\t                ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\n    70\\\\t  sorry\\\\n    71\\\\t\\\\n    72\\\\t/-- Construction of the extended-line measurements with the estimate actually\\\\n    73\\\\tdelivered by the first proof route, `C * m * poly(epsilon, md / q)`.\\\\n    74\\\\t\\\\n    75\\\\tThis is an established auxiliary form of the argument, not the source-labelled\\\\n    76\\\\t`lem:qld-4-13`; it must not be advertised as that theorem.  The source discrepancy\\\\n    77\\\\tis analyzed in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex`.  As in the\\\\n    78\\\\tsource-facing declaration, the extended questions use the directly indexed line-space\\\\n    79\\\\tconstruction.  This conditional declaration takes an already constructed point witness;\\\\n    80\\\\tthe source-facing construction below supplies it existentially.  Relating its game to the source's\\\\n    81\\\\tseed-bearing game requires the transport\\\\n    82\\\\tand soundness obligations in\\\\n    83\\\\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`.\\\\n    84\\\\t-/\\\\n    85\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness_established_ofPointsWitness :\\\\n    86\\\\t    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧\\\\n    87\\\\t      ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\n    88\\\\t        ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε δQ : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε)\\\\n    89\\\\t          (points : CombinedPointsWitness S δQ),\\\\n    90\\\\t          Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\n    91\\\\t            (C * (P.m : ℝ) *\\\\n    92\\\\t              deltaCombine ε ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\n    93\\\\t  sorry\\\\n    94\\\\t\\\\n    95\\\\t/-- Source-facing construction for the established auxiliary estimate.  This is\\\\n    96\\\\tthe same Lean-only bound as `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established_ofPointsWitness`,\\\\n    97\\\\twith the point witness existentially supplied rather than assumed. -/\\\\n    98\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness_established :\\\\n    99\\\\t    ∃ deltaQ : ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr deltaQ ∧\\\\n   100\\\\t      ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧\\\\n   101\\\\t        ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\n   102\\\\t          ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε),\\\\n   103\\\\t            ∃ points : CombinedPointsWitness S (deltaQ ε),\\\\n   104\\\\t              Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\n   105\\\\t                (C * (P.m : ℝ) *\\\\n   106\\\\t                  deltaCombine ε ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\n   107\\\\t  sorry\\\\n   108\\\\t\\\\n   109\\\\t/-- Construction of the projective global polynomial-pair measurements from\\\\n   110\\\\t`lem:qld-4-7`, paper lines 1267--1274.  The statement has the source's universal\\\\n   111\\\\tconstants and contains no divisibility hypothesis or residual construction input.\\\\n   112\\\\t\\\\n   113\\\\tThe argument uses low-degree soundness at dimension `2 * m + 2`.  The current\\\\n   114\\\\tdirect carrier realizes the required dimension without assuming\\\\n   115\\\\t`2 * m + 2 ∣ q`, but it does not itself prove the game-correspondence and\\\\n   116\\\\tauxiliary-parameter estimates required by the soundness import; those obligations\\\\n   117\\\\tare exposed by `exists_direct_ld_soundness` and documented in\\\\n   118\\\\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`.  Absorption of the established\\\\n   119\\\\tcombined-lines prefactor into the final universal constants is to use\\\\n   120\\\\t`deltaQld_mono` on its stated source parameter domain.\\\\n   121\\\\t-/\\\\n   122\\\\ttheorem exists_globalPairWitness :\\\\n   123\\\\t    ∃ a b : ℝ, 1 < a ∧ 0 < b ∧ b < 1 ∧\\\\n   124\\\\t      ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε →\\\\n   125\\\\t        ∀ S : ProjectiveSetting P ε,\\\\n   126\\\\t          Nonempty (GlobalPairWitness S (deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q)) := by\\\\n   127\\\\t  sorry\\\\n   128\\\\t\\\\n   129\\\\tend\\\\n   130\\\\t\\\\n   131\\\\tend MIPStarRE.QPBT\\\\n   250\\\\t  /-- Each line triple carries affine data sufficient for\\\\n   251\\\\t  `combineLinePoly_spec`. -/\\\\n   252\\\\t  compatibility : ∀ sample ∈ D.support,\\\\n   253\\\\t    ∃ aX bX aZ bZ uAlpha vAlpha uBeta vBeta : PauliScalar P,\\\\n   254\\\\t      IsCombineLineCompatible\\\\n   255\\\\t        (directPointToPauli P sample.1.base)\\\\n   256\\\\t        (directPointToPauli P sample.1.direction)\\\\n   257\\\\t        sample.2.1.base sample.2.1.direction\\\\n   258\\\\t        sample.2.2.base sample.2.2.direction\\\\n   259\\\\t        aX bX aZ bZ uAlpha vAlpha uBeta vBeta\\\\n   260\\\\t  /-- Each one-point projected marginal is a mixture of restricted product\\\\n   261\\\\t  laws.  No equality for their joint conditional law is claimed. -/\\\\n   262\\\\t  source_mixture : ∃ components : Distribution (SubLineComponent P),\\\\n   263\\\\t    components.IsProbability ∧\\\\n   264\\\\t      (subLinePointDist P D).map subLineXProjection =\\\\n   265\\\\t        Distribution.bind components (subLineXComponentDist P) ∧\\\\n   266\\\\t      (subLinePointDist P D).map subLineZProjection =\\\\n   267\\\\t        Distribution.bind components (subLineZComponentDist P)\\\\n   268\\\\t  /-- An extended axis line has axis-parallel projected lines. -/\\\\n   269\\\\t  axis_closure : ∀ sample ∈ D.support, sample.1.kind = .axis ->\\\\n   270\\\\t    sample.2.1.kind = .axis ∧ sample.2.2.kind = .axis\\\\n   271\\\\t\\\\n   272\\\\t/-! ## Extended lines and global polynomial pairs -/\\\\n   273\\\\t\\\\n   274\\\\t/-- Extended-line POVMs and the two source consistency displays from\\\\n   275\\\\t`lem:qld-4-13`, paper lines 1020--1034.  The direct line carrier avoids the\\\\n   276\\\\tdimension-divisibility obstruction documented in\\\\n   277\\\\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`. -/\\\\n   278\\\\tstructure ExtendedLinesWitness {P : AdmissibleParams} {ε δQ : ℝ}\\\\n   279\\\\t    (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε) (points : CombinedPointsWitness S δQ)\\\\n   280\\\\t    (δ : ℝ) where\\\\n   281\\\\t  /-- The complete extended-line measurement on each player side. -/\\\\n   282\\\\t  Qline : (side : PlayerSide) -> DirectLineDesc P.extendedDirectLd ->\\\\n   283\\\\t    Measurement (DirectDegPoly P.extendedDirectLd (P.m * P.d + 1))\\\\n   284\\\\t      (S.ExpandedLocalSpace side)\\\\n   285\\\\t  /-- Axis-line outcomes outside degree `d` have zero effect. -/\\\\n   286\\\\t  axis_degree : ∀ side line f, line.kind = .axis ->\\\\n   287\\\\t    Not (∀ i, P.d < i.val -> f i = 0) ->\\\\n   288\\\\t      (Qline side line).effect f = 0\\\\n   289\\\\t  /-- Alice's evaluated line measurement is consistent with Bob's completed\\\\n   290\\\\t  combined point measurement. -/\\\\n   291\\\\t  consistent_alice : consistencyDefect\\\\n   292\\\\t    (directLinePointDist P.extendedDirectLd)\\\\n   293\\\\t    (fun sample answer => S.place .AA'\\\\n   294\\\\t      (((Qline .alice sample.1).postprocess\\\\n   295\\\\t        (fun f => (directEvalOpt sample.1 sample.2 f).map\\\\n   296\\\\t          (extendedDirectScalarEquiv P))).effect answer))\\\\n   297\\\\t    (fun sample answer => S.place .BA''\\\\n   298\\\\t      (((points.Q .bob\\\\n   299\\\\t        (projX (directPointToPauli P sample.2))\\\\n   300\\\\t        (projZ (directPointToPauli P sample.2))).postprocess fun ab =>\\\\n   301\\\\t          some (directPointToPauli P sample.2 (alphaVar P.m) * ab.1 +\\\\n   302\\\\t            directPointToPauli P sample.2 (betaVar P.m) * ab.2)).effect answer))\\\\n   303\\\\t    S.psiHat <= δ\\\\n   304\\\\t  /-- Bob's evaluated line measurement is consistent with Alice's completed\\\\n   305\\\\t  combined point measurement. -/\\\\n   306\\\\t  consistent_bob : consistencyDefect\\\\n   307\\\\t    (directLinePointDist P.extendedDirectLd)\\\\n   308\\\\t    (fun sample answer => S.place .BB'\\\\n   309\\\\t      (((Qline .bob sample.1).postprocess\\\\n   310\\\\t        (fun f => (directEvalOpt sample.1 sample.2 f).map\\\\n   311\\\\t          (extendedDirectScalarEquiv P))).effect answer))\\\\n   312\\\\t    (fun sample answer => S.place .AB''\\\\n   313\\\\t      (((points.Q .alice\\\\n   314\\\\t        (projX (directPointToPauli P sample.2))\\\\n   315\\\\t        (projZ (directPointToPauli P sample.2))).postprocess fun ab =>\\\\n   316\\\\t          some (directPointToPauli P sample.2 (alphaVar P.m) * ab.1 +\\\\n   317\\\\t            directPointToPauli P sample.2 (betaVar P.m) * ab.2)).effect answer))\\\\n   318\\\\t    S.psiHat <= δ\\\\n   319\\\\t\\\\n   320\\\\t/-- The side-indexed global polynomial-pair measurements handed to Chapter 16.\\\\n   321\\\\tThis is the exact conclusion of `lem:qld-4-7`, paper lines 1267--1274, with\\\\n   322\\\\tthe two heterogeneous point-consistency displays stated separately. -/\\\\n   323\\\\tstructure GlobalPairWitness {P : AdmissibleParams} {ε : ℝ}\\\\n   324\\\\t    (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε) (δ : ℝ) where\\\\n   325\\\\t  /-- The complete global polynomial-pair measurement on each player side. -/\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-372-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_190\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex | sed -n '1800,1925p'\\\\nrg -n -A35 -B15 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lem:qld-4-7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex | tail -n 90\\\\nrg -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0 *[<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\le]+ *\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps|eps.*[01]|epsilon\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex | head -n 30\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-373-{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_190\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex | sed -n '1800,1925p'\\\\nrg -n -A35 -B15 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lem:qld-4-7\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex | tail -n 90\\\\nrg -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0 *[<\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\le]+ *\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps|eps.*[01]|epsilon\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex | head -n 30\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"  1800\\\\t\\\\tunder the answer summation over $a \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q$ used above. Relating the two\\\\n  1801\\\\t\\\\tformulations is the transport obligation of\\\\n  1802\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}.\\\\n  1803\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n  1804\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{proof}\\\\n  1805\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{lem:qld-xz-lines, lem:qld-sublines, def:combine-map,\\\\n  1806\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tlem:qld-4-12, lem:claim-17-1, lem:claim-17-2, lem:claim-17-3}\\\\n  1807\\\\t\\\\tThis is what the proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-13} above establishes: the\\\\n  1808\\\\t\\\\tchaining of the three claims bounds\\\\n  1809\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency} by\\\\n  1810\\\\t\\\\t$O(m(\\\\\\\\eps^{1/4} + \\\\\\\\delta_P^{1/4} + \\\\\\\\delta_Q^{1/4} +\\\\n  1811\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2}))$, a function of the form\\\\n  1812\\\\t\\\\t$m \\\\\\\\cdot \\\\\\\\poly(\\\\\\\\eps, md/q)$, and the remaining steps of that proof are\\\\n  1813\\\\t\\\\tunchanged.\\\\n  1814\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{proof}\\\\n  1815\\\\t\\\\n  1816\\\\tThe measurements of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-12} and Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}\\\\n  1817\\\\tconstitute a strategy for the classical low individual degree game in $2m+2$\\\\n  1818\\\\tvariables. Applying the quantum soundness of that game yields a single\\\\n  1819\\\\tprojective measurement whose outcomes are pairs of global polynomials.\\\\n  1820\\\\t\\\\n  1821\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[The global polynomial-pair measurement]\\\\n  1822\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-4-7}\\\\n  1823\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Poly, MIPStarRE.QPBT.PolyPair, MIPStarRE.QPBT.evalAt}\\\\n  1824\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.GlobalPairWitness}\\\\n  1825\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_globalPairWitness}\\\\n  1826\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\notready\\\\n  1827\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:polyfunc, def:expanded-state, def:expanded-point-measurement,\\\\n  1828\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tdef:consistency, def:bracket, def:ideg-deg-polynomials}\\\\n  1829\\\\t\\\\t% Statement as in the source (references/qpbt-paper/\\\\n  1830\\\\t\\\\t% 14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex, lem:qld-4-7). The proof\\\\n  1831\\\\t\\\\t% instantiates the classical low individual degree game, and Theorem\\\\n  1832\\\\t\\\\t% lem:ld-soundness, at dimension 2m+2, which def:ld-game admits only\\\\n  1833\\\\t\\\\t% when the dimension divides q; the source performs the instantiation\\\\n  1834\\\\t\\\\t% without securing this condition. See rem:qld-4-7-divisibility.\\\\n  1835\\\\t\\\\tThere exists a function\\\\n  1836\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\delta_S(\\\\\\\\eps,m,d,q) = a(md)^a(\\\\\\\\eps^b + q^{-b} + 2^{-bmd})$, for some\\\\n  1837\\\\t\\\\tuniversal constants $a > 1$ and $0 < b < 1$, such that the following\\\\n  1838\\\\t\\\\tholds. For\\\\n  1839\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\hilb \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{\\\\\\\\hilb_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{A}}, \\\\\\\\hilb_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{B}}\\\\\\\\}$ there\\\\n  1840\\\\t\\\\texists a projective measurement $\\\\\\\\{\\\\\\\\hat{S}_{g_X,g_Z}\\\\\\\\}$ acting on\\\\n  1841\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\hilb \\\\\