 :\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:31:\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.decodeFq_add, MIPStarRE.QPBT.decodeFq_smul, MIPStarRE.QPBT.decodeFq_lowDegreeEncoding}\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:403:\\\\t\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_extractionWitness}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl:387:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_198\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"## Findings\\\\n\\\\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:806` — `\\\\\\\\notready` is stale because `exists_combinedPointsWitness` has the same source-shaped statement without a proof-debt input.\\\\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:44` — The decoder proof omits `def:decoding-map` from `\\\\\\\\uses` although Lean directly applies `decodeAt_lowDegreeEnc`.\\\\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Apply.lean:95` — The newly linked directly indexed auxiliary is still called “Source-facing” and named by proof status, contradicting the audited carrier, distribution, and outcome differences.\\\\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Extraction/Unitary.lean:75` — The conditional extraction theorem still calls itself source-facing despite requiring a `GlobalPairWitness`.\\\\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:786` — The proof sketch uses Lean and progress-report language instead of directly presenting the relabelling argument.\\\\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:272` — “provider-side correction” and “provider-side normalization defect” are software terminology rather than mathematical attribution.\\\\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1786` — The support lemma narrates graph and tag status using “node”, “formalization mark”, and “linked declaration”.\\\\n- [ ] F8 (changes